  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mstorage.js[39m   │ The seam. Persist and retrieve. Knows nothing about UI or rules.             │ nothing           │
  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mtasks.js[39m     │ Domain state + the [38;5;153mapplyChange[39m chokepoint. Validation, timestamps,           │ [38;5;153mstorage.js[39m        │
  │              │ subscriber notification.                                                     │                   │
  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mrender.js[39m    │ Takes a task array, produces DOM into [38;5;153m<main>[39m. No mutation, no storage.       │ nothing           │
  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mreminders.js[39m │ The tick. Finds due-and-unnotified tasks, fires, marks them.                 │ [38;5;153mtasks.js[39m,         │
  │              │                                                                              │ [38;5;153mnotify.js[39m         │
  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mnotify.js[39m    │ Browser Notification API, with an in-app banner fallback.                    │ nothing           │
  ├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mmain.js[39m      │ Wiring and bootstrap. The only file that knows all the others exist.         │ all               │
  └──────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────┘

  [1mData flow[0m is a single loop, and every mutation takes the same path:

  user event → applyChange(type, payload)
                 ├─ validate
                 ├─ stamp updatedAt
                 ├─ persist via storage.put / storage.remove
                 ├─ update in-memory array
                 └─ emit "changed"
                      ├─→ render.js re-renders <main> from state
                      └─→ (phase 2: change notifications hook here)

  [38;5;153mreminders.js[39m also calls [38;5;153mapplyChange[39m when it sets [38;5;153mnotifiedAt[39m, so even the reminder system's own writes go through the
  one chokepoint — no back door. That's what makes the chokepoint a real invariant rather than a convention, and it's
  why phase 2 has exactly one place to plug into.

  Does this hold up? The piece most worth arguing about is the async storage interface, since it's the one bit of
  visible overhead you'll pay for in every call site of phase 1 to buy an option in a phase that might not happen.

